gates.prompt:
Brainstorm for: {{topic}}
Constraints: {{constraints}} | Horizon: {{horizon}}
Angle: NOMINAL — the obvious, natural approach. Generate 3-5 concrete ideas. No filtering.
Return JSON: { "angle": "nominal", "ideas": [{"title": "", "description": "", "key_assumption": ""}] }

Brainstorm for: {{topic}}
Constraints: {{constraints}} | Horizon: {{horizon}}
Angle: ALTERNATIVE — the opposite or radically different approach. What if you did the reverse?
Return JSON: { "angle": "alternative", "ideas": [{"title": "", "description": "", "key_assumption": ""}] }

Brainstorm for: {{topic}}
Constraints: {{constraints}} | Horizon: {{horizon}}
Angle: SEVERE CONSTRAINTS — half the time, 10% budget, minimal team. Absolute MVP only.
Return JSON: { "angle": "constrained", "ideas": [{"title": "", "description": "", "key_assumption": ""}] }

Brainstorm for: {{topic}}
Constraints: {{constraints}} | Horizon: {{horizon}}
Angle: FUTURE REGRET — in 1 year, what will you wish you had done now? What short-term thinking will you regret?
Return JSON: { "angle": "future", "ideas": [{"title": "", "description": "", "key_assumption": ""}] }

Pre-mortem for: {{topic}}
It is 6 months from now. The plan failed.
Your assigned failure category (by instance index 0-4): technical | user | platform | dependencies | scope
From your category's perspective, what went wrong?
Return JSON: { "category": "", "risks": [{"description": "", "probability": "high|medium|low", "impact": "critical|moderate|minor", "mitigation": ""}] }

Synthesize brainstorming and pre-mortem for: {{topic}}

Ideas collected:
- Nominal: {{ideator-nominal.ideas}}
- Alternative: {{ideator-alternative.ideas}}
- Constrained: {{ideator-constrained.ideas}}
- Future: {{ideator-future.ideas}}

Risks from pre-mortem: {{premortem-analyst.risks}}

Produce:
1. top_ideas: best 2-3 ideas with rationale
2. critical_risks: top 3 risks with mitigations
3. unknowns: what we don't know yet
4. success_criterion: one measurable signal of success
5. mvp_if_halved: scope if time is cut in half
6. verdict: READY_TO_PLAN | NEEDS_INVESTIGATION | STOP
7. verdict_reason: one sentence
